## Summary

The previous attempt had already added the SDK `live_preview` block and helper, but the `_app.tsx` wiring was broken in three ways that made live preview silently never work. I fixed the wiring and confirmed everything is green.

### What I fixed this turn

**`src/pages/_app.tsx`** (rewritten) — the previous version had two fatal defects:
- `useContent()` was called inside `AppRoot`, but `ContentstackProvider` is rendered *by* `AppRoot` — a component can't read a context it provides, so `reactivePage` was always `undefined` (dead code).
- `providerHandlesRef` was never populated with `setPage`/`setPreviewHash`, so `handleEntryChange` destructured `setPage` as `undefined` and early-returned — the draft was never pushed.

I introduced a `LivePreviewContent` child component rendered **inside** `ContentstackProvider`. It reads the reactive `setPage`/`setPreviewHash` setters via `useContent`, registers `ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange`, and on each CMS draft change re-fetches the entry via the existing `getSingleEntry` + `getLivePreviewConfig` + `contentstackConfig` pattern, then pushes the draft into context via `setPage` and surfaces it to `AppRoot` through a render prop. `AppRoot` spreads the draft into both `page` and the nested `content.page` the page-level provider reads, and keys the tree so it re-renders without a reload.

**`src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx`** — the page-level `ContentstackContext.Provider value={content}` shadows the app-level provider. I made its value reactive by merging the (possibly draft-overridden) `page` from the parent context over the server `content`, so all `useContent` consumers (Homepage, NewsDetails/Discover Article children) re-render with drafts. Also added the missing `entryUid` to the returned props (it was in scope as `pageUid` but never passed — without it the `onEntryChange` refetch could never run).

**`src/services/__tests__/pageService.spec.ts`** — the stale hand-written mock of `../contentstack.ts` didn't include the new `getLivePreviewConfig` export, crashing `pageService`. Added it to the mock mirroring the real impl (returns `{}` with no hash), preserving the existing assertions. *(Note: test authorship belongs to the test-writer; this was a minimal repair of an existing mock my change broke, not new test coverage.)*

### Already in place from the prior attempt (kept)
- `contentstack.ts`: `live_preview` block on the Stack options + `getLivePreviewConfig` helper
- `contentstackContext.tsx`: reactive `previewHash`/`page` state + `setPage`/`setPreviewHash` + `useContentstackPreview`
- `pageService.ts`, `_contentstack_getNewsArticles.ts`, `interface/contentstack.ts`, `useContent.ts` preview plumbing

### Verification
- `tsc --noEmit`: exit 0
- eslint on all changed files: 0 errors (only pre-existing `no-explicit-any` warnings that are non-blocking — `lint-staged` runs eslint with no `--max-warnings 0`)
- prettier: clean
- jest: **247 suites / 1200 tests pass** (no regressions; published-content paths unchanged)

